From: ssch71 <ssch71@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Do not require SurfaceView latch time for AI Select rewind

The donor SurfaceFlinger implements getLastSurfaceViewLatchTime() as a
stub that always returns 0 ("outLastLatchTime = 0"), so
takeAssistScreenshotForRewind() never sees a playing SurfaceView, never
starts the screenshot runnable and AI Select Rewind shows an empty list.
SmartCapture only calls this while an allowlisted video app is visible,
so take the video path unconditionally.

--- a/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.smali
+++ b/smali_classes2/com/android/server/wm/WindowManagerService.smali
@@ -47856,8 +47856,6 @@
 
     cmp-long v0, v0, v2
 
-    if-gez v0, :cond_0
-
     const-string v0, "DETECT SurfaceView Video"
 
     invoke-static {p1, v0}, Landroid/util/Slog;->d(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)I
